Some more suggestions:
   How about a dragon that has more than one type of breath?

   Also, it would make the dungeon more interesting(and challenging) if there
are rooms that can cancel intrinics.  For example, a fire room 
will cancel your intrinic fire resistance and make you vulnerable
to fire attacks.  Furthermore, if you do not have the resistance
to start with, fire attacks can cause you extra damage.  Using
a wand of cold in a fire room should also have some interesting
effects.

   Give some powerful monsters the displacement intrinic, perhaps
by displaying them a square away from their actual location.  
Maybe using a mirror on displaced monster will show their
true locations for a short amount of time.

    Telepathy(the floating eye kind) 
should not reveal the locations of monsters close by.
Currently there are not a whole lot of reasons not to be blind
when possessing telepathy.

   Vampire lords should be able to regenerate(resurrect) themselves
in a darkened room.  They should also be able to wield weapons and      
wear capes(cloaks?).

   Resurrected monsters should become more powerful( lower AC class;
higher Exp; immunity from the type of magic, if any, that killed it)
to prevent the player from killing it again and again,
endlessly.

   Give some powerful monsters in Hell rings of regeneration
and rings of shock resistance.  Currently Mjollnir is so powerful that 
most monsters don't stand a chance (in Hell).   Better yet, 
give them rings of see invisible, rings of cold/fire/foo/bar resistance;
perhaps even a ring of drain level protection to protect against
Stormbringer.

